From 3b61d110295479a06e67544f21667117c60b9164 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: koldfrontier <koldfrontier@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 03:07:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Require the DSML token for DeepSeek V4.1 tool call markup
 (#65019)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Base: 1107 vLLM patch head b9276542af6feba1b8f916b521f857cd23bd1224 (upstream 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354 + 641 patches).

Rationale:
In the DeepSeek V4.1 tokenizer, 128825 (｜DSML｜) is a bare atom token while each full DSML tag (<｜DSML｜ calls>, <｜DSML｜ invoke name="...", <｜DSML｜ parameter name="..." string="...">, and their closing tags) is a composite sequence of ordinary text tokens around 128825. Because the model can also spell "｜DSML｜" out of ordinary text tokens when quoting DSML markup in prose or writing files containing DSML strings (issues #876 and #948), text-only matching treats quoted DSML tags as genuine structural markers:
- A quoted DSML block in a normal assistant reply is parsed into tool_calls or silently swallowed when the function name is not in request.tools (#876).
- A literal "</｜DSML｜ parameter>" or "</｜DSML｜ calls>" inside a string tool argument truncates the parameter value or closes the tool call early (#948).
- An untrusted "<｜DSML｜ parameter ...>" tag after a closed parameter arms the 0643 incremental open-value extender and appends subsequent text into the closed parameter.
- Splitting "<｜DSML｜ calls>" across streaming deltas when reasoning ends implicitly loses the token-origin span across separate reasoning/tool parser instances in DelegatingParser.
- Formatting newlines between "</｜DSML｜ invoke>" and "</｜DSML｜ calls>" in TOOL_BETWEEN leak into assistant content when non-whitespace content preceded the tool block.
- When --tool-call-parser deepseek_v41 or --reasoning-parser deepseek_v41 is configured alone, falling back to DelegatingParser drops model_output_token_ids in non-streaming parse() and leaves ParserEngine in ParserState.REASONING when skip_reasoning_parsing=True.

Track token-ID origin spans through TokenIDScanner, IncrementalLexer, StreamingParserEngine, and ToolCallSlot:
- Gate composite DSML terminals (TOOL_START, TOOL_END, INVOKE_PREFIX, INVOKE_END, PARAM_START, PARAM_CLOSE) on the presence of a genuine 128825 token span at the "｜DSML｜" offset.
- Filter parameter header and close matches in DeepSeekV41Parser (_dsml_arg_converter and _dsml_open_value_extender) by recorded token-origin spans, holding back partial genuine headers during incremental string streaming.
- Route both parse() and parse_delta() through DeepSeekV41ServingParser whenever either --reasoning-parser deepseek_v41 or --tool-call-parser deepseek_v41 is active, and start ParserEngine in ParserState.CONTENT when skip_reasoning_parsing=True, preserving token provenance in combined, tool-only, and reasoning-only configurations while keeping DSML markup as content when tools are absent or tool_choice="none".
- Hold back pure whitespace in TOOL_BETWEEN unless non-whitespace text follows in the same span so structural newlines between "</｜DSML｜ invoke>" and "</｜DSML｜ calls>" do not append to pre-tool assistant content.
- Include prompt turn-boundary reasoning checks (set_prompt_token_ids, #61857) so multi-turn and task prompts do not inherit an earlier turn's "</think>".

Quality:
Sampling-neutral; affects only post-generation output parsing for --reasoning-parser deepseek_v41 and --tool-call-parser deepseek_v41. Preserves bit-identical outputs on clean replies while preventing false tool-call extraction and argument truncation when replies or string arguments quote DSML markup.

Tests:
- pytest tests/parser/engine/test_deepseek_v41_dsml_provenance.py (86 passed)
- pytest tests/tool_parsers/test_deepseekv41_tool_parser.py (152 passed)
- pytest tests/parser/engine/test_deepseek_v41.py tests/parser/engine/test_deepseek_v4.py tests/parser/engine/test_token_id_scanner.py tests/parser/engine/test_parser_engine.py tests/tool_parsers/test_deepseekv4_tool_parser.py tests/tool_parsers/test_deepseekv32_tool_parser.py (389 passed; 627 total passed across 2 container boots)
- replay_fixtures.py on fixtures/live-1030.json and fixtures/live-1030-thinking.json (all 9 cases pass across whole, stream/1, stream/7, stream/10000 across 2 container boots)

Upstream status: backported from https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/65019 (with #61857 prompt reasoning state hook) and adapted to the 1107 series.
